<%# locals: (title:, items: [], focus: true, data: {}, id: nil, css: nil) -%>
<%# The one error box. Locals: title; items (list of [text, anchor] where anchor is a field id or nil); focus (default
    true: the browser moves focus here on a refused submit, so a keyboard user lands on it; pass false where a
    controller already does that); data (extra data attributes); id; css (a placement class from the page, for example the admin forms
    pass admin-form__errors so the box is as wide as the form card under it). Announced on render (role=alert). The caller
    decides whether to show it. -%>
<%= tag.div class: [ "alert alert--danger error-summary", css ], role: "alert", tabindex: -1, autofocus: (focus || nil), id: id, data: data do %>
  <p class="alert__title"><%= title %></p>
  <% if items.any? %>
    <ul>
      <% items.each do |text, anchor| %>
        <li>
          <% if anchor %>
            <a href="#<%= anchor %>"><%= text %></a>
          <% else %>
            <%= text %>
          <% end %>
        </li>
      <% end %>
    </ul>
  <% end %>
<% end %>
